  "reply": "I rewrote `parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts`, and `bun test` now passes all 26 tests. I changed no other files and kept the public export as it was.\n\n- **Accepted input:** one or more nonnegative integer components in strictly descending `h`, `m`, `s`, `ms` order. Whitespace is allowed between components and at both ends.\n- **Rejected with `RangeError`:** empty or whitespace-only input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions, junk, and whitespace between a number and its unit (the existing `\"1 s\"` test requires this). Any component or running total above `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` is also rejected.\n- **Whole-input check:** the parser has to consume the entire string, so a partial parse is never accepted.\n- **Constraint:** no dependencies were added.",
